We're back online.  The heat pump died during a decent heatwave, but the old house managed to show it's worth.
The double brick walls kept the interior cool in, and we would air the house down over night.  not perfect, but managable.  We'll need a new idea for the heat pump however....
Canada Day saw massive storms and winds; we ended up taking shelter in the root cellar incase of Tornado proper.  In the end, the house stood still.  we lose several big old trees, including a limb from our 200 year old Apple tree, which is a shame.
A tornado touched down North East of us, and many people lost trees.  the grid was down for about 60 hours.  We lost a fridge of food, but are none the worse for wear.

This has led me to determine we cannot rely on the grid, as it fails around here every 6 months.  Im working on a plan for central heating/cooling, which is extensive addition.  AND now we have to consider making our own energy in a grid down scnario at least.

And then last night the shower mixer cartridge stuck.  ive had to replace the whole thing
